<.shell title="Layout" current={:layout}>
  <h1>Layout</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Eight spaces on a 4px grid, a page header every page shares, and blocks to group content.
  </p>

  <h2>Spacing scale</h2>
  <p>
    Margins, padding, and gaps come from these eight. Tokens are <code>--sp-1</code>
    to <code>--sp-8</code>.
  </p>
  <.table id="spacing" rows={spacing()}>
    <:col :let={{step, _px, _use}} label="Token" class="w-px mono">sp-{step}</:col>
    <:col :let={{_step, px, _use}} label="Size" class="w-px" align="right">{px}px</:col>
    <:col :let={{_step, _px, use}} label="Typical use">{use}</:col>
    <:col :let={{_step, px, _use}} label="">
      <span class="space-bar" style={"width: #{px}px"}></span>
    </:col>
  </.table>

  <h2>Page header</h2>
  <p>Breadcrumbs, then the title.</p>
  <div class="demo">
    <.breadcrumbs team={sample_team()}>
      <:item label="Activities" path="#" />
      <:item label="25-0412" />
    </.breadcrumbs>
    <h1 class="title">Missing hiker, Stawamus Chief</h1>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;.breadcrumbs&gt;</code>, then an <code>h1</code>
    with <code>class="title"</code>. A page's actions sit with its content, not in the header.
  </p>

  <h2>Detail list</h2>
  <p>Key facts about one record, as on an activity's or a member's page.</p>
  <div class="demo max-w-100">
    <dl>
      <dt>Kind</dt>
      <dd><.activity_badges activity={hd(activities())} /></dd>
      <dt>Attendance</dt>
      <dd>14 members · 62h 15m in total</dd>
      <dt>Start</dt>
      <dd>
        {Service.Format.datetime_medium(hd(activities()).started_at, sample_team().timezone)}
      </dd>
      <dt>Finish</dt>
      <dd>
        {Service.Format.datetime_medium(hd(activities()).finished_at, sample_team().timezone)}
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: a plain <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code>. Each <code>dd</code> gets a rule under it.
  </p>

  <h2>Stats</h2>
  <p>
    A few numbers at the top of a dashboard. See <a href={page_path(:charts)}>Charts and maps</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="chart-stats">
      <.stat value="47" label="Activities in 2025" delta="Up 6 on this time last year" />
      <.stat value="1,204h" label="Member hours" />
      <.stat value="12" label="Letters to create" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Card</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <section class="dash-card">
      <header>
        <h2 class="chart-title">D4H connection</h2>
        <span class="text-sm text-secondary-1">Last refreshed today at 02:00</span>
      </header>
      <p class="paragraph">833 members, 1,912 activities.</p>
      <.button size={:sm}>
        <.icon name="hero-arrow-path-micro" class="size-4" /> Refresh now
      </.button>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;section class="dash-card"&gt;</code>, as on the team's home page.
  </p>

  <h2>Details</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <details class="disclosure">
      <summary>
        <.icon name="hero-chevron-down-micro" class="size-4" />Why are some members missing?
      </summary>
      <div>
        SAR Duty copies members from D4H each night. Members added in D4H today show up tomorrow, or
        after a manual refresh.
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
  <p class="spec not-yet">
    Not used in the app yet: <code>&lt;details class="disclosure"&gt;</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Page width</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Content fills up to 1280px; tables use the full width.</li>
    <li>Text and forms stop at 640 to 800px, so lines stay readable.</li>
    <li>Desktop first. On a phone, layouts stack and wide tables scroll sideways.</li>
  </ul>
</.shell>
